":{"type":"boolean"},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"]},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"description":"The PEOPLE-pool filter this CRM audience is bound to: every serve draws from the brand's merged people (everyone its connected tools know, one row per human) who match it, instead of from imported files. null = not people-bound (file-bound via crmUploadId, or the whole imported list)."},"crmPeopleByStage":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"pipeline":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"stage":{"type":"string"},"served":{"type":"integer"},"remainingSendable":{"type":"integer"},"totalSendable":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["pipeline","stage","served","remainingSendable","totalSendable"]},"description":"A people-bound CRM audience whose segment names dealStages: crm-service's counts per stated stage (same snapshot as Size / Remaining). Entries overlap when a person holds deals at two of them. null otherwise."},"offerId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The offer (Org > Brand > Offer > Campaign) this audience belongs to — an id owned by brand-service. An audience is assembled for one distinct thing the brand sells, so it is scoped to that offer rather than to every offer of the brand. null = no offer stated ⟹ the audience is brand-wide, the pre-existing behaviour."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["suggested","active","paused","archived","deprecated"],"description":"Always 'suggested' (inactive) for a freshly-suggested audience."},"source":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"profileAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The client PROFILE (WHO, a cold audience the client keeps or pauses on the Targeting page) this source list was built for: a buying-signal list (hiring now, new in role, recently funded) or a competitor-post engagement list finds THAT profile's people, screened against the profile's text. Pausing or archiving the profile pauses its lists; resuming it resumes them (unless the source itself is off). null on a profile itself, on a whole-ICP list built before profiles had their own (retired once they do), and on every other audience. Show profiles = rows with null here and channels[0].list = apollo_search; sources = channels[0].list."},"role":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["target","search",null],"description":"AUDIENCE-PER-OFFER-1107. 'target' = THE audience of its offer: its text is who the offer targets, it has no list of its own and finds people through the brand's lists, each person judged against its text. 'search' = a list of the brand (Apollo search, signals, engagement) walked by every offer audience of it; hidden from GET /orgs/audiences unless role=search. null = an audience as before."},"canonicalAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"When this audience is a deprecated provider-variant (e.g. retired '<base> [Apify]' from the apify->apollo migration), the id of its active canonical replacement. Membership/stats reads resolve a deprecated match to this audience. null for non-deprecated / unlinked rows."},"filters":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"avatarUrl":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Audience avatar as a hosted HTTP(S) URL. null until generated."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"countedAt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"degraded":{"type":"boolean","description":"The chooser's verdict on the audience it picked for this row: true when no attempt apollo-service explored really answered the request and the least-bad one was chosen anyway. INFORMATION for the customer and the dashboard — nothing here blocks, filters or warns on it, and an audience is always chosen. false for rows created before the flag existed and whenever the chooser judged the pick a genuine answer."},"createdByUserId":{"type":"string"","note":"Narrow the request (a filter, a limit, one id) to read the rest."}}],"needsTheirYes":false}
